.\" vi: set sw=4 ts=4:
.TH MY_FS 1 "2026-05-11" "BusyBox Diagnostic Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
my_fs \- filesystem health checker: disk usage, inode analysis, and fragmentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B my_fs
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIPATH\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B my_fs
displays disk space usage and health information for one or more filesystems.
Without path arguments, it reads
.I /proc/mounts
and reports all mounted physical filesystems (de-duplicated by
.IR st_dev ,
virtual filesystems with
.I f_blocks
== 0 are excluded).
.PP
Core features:
.IP \(bu 2
Disk usage analysis compatible with GNU
.BR df (1)
output format
.IP \(bu 2
Inode usage analysis compatible with
.B df \-i
.IP \(bu 2
Dual-perspective Use% with root-reserved block information (Use%(user) and
Use%(real) side by side)
.IP \(bu 2
Per-file FIEMAP extent analysis compatible with util-linux
.BR filefrag (1)
.IP \(bu 2
Mount-point fragmentation statistics via
.BR nftw (3)
traversal with Top-N most fragmented files
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive TUI live-monitoring mode
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Human-readable sizes.
Capacity values are automatically scaled to K/M/G/T with ceiling round-up,
matching the behavior of
.BR df \-h .
.TP
.B \-i
Inode mode.
Displays Inodes / IUsed / IFree / IUse% instead of block counts,
matching
.BR df \-i .
.TP
.B \-r
Dual-perspective reserved-block mode.
Adds Use%(user), Use%(real), and RootResv columns to the output,
making it immediately visible why
.B df
may show 100% while the system is still operational.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR \fITYPE\fR
Show only filesystems of the given type (e.g.\& ext4, tmpfs).
Matches the behavior of
.BR df \-t .
.TP
\fB\-x\fR \fITYPE\fR
Exclude filesystems of the given type.
Matches the behavior of
.BR df \-x .
.TP
\fB\-f\fR \fIFILE\fR
Run a FIEMAP
.BR ioctl (2)
on the specified regular file and print all extents with their logical and
physical offsets and lengths (in filesystem blocks).
Output format is compatible with
.BR "filefrag \-v" .
Filesystems that do not support FIEMAP (e.g.\& tmpfs, overlayfs) produce an
error message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-F\fR \fIPATH\fR
Scan all regular files under the given mount point using
.BR nftw (3)
and report fragmentation statistics: distribution by extent count
(1 / 2-4 / 5-16 / 17+) and the Top 10 most fragmented files.
.TP
.B \-s
Interactive TUI mode.
Clears the screen and refreshes all mount-point statistics once per second.
.RS
.PP
Key bindings:
.TP
.B D
Switch to disk capacity view (default)
.TP
.B I
Switch to inode view
.TP
.B R
Switch to dual Use% / reserved-block view
.TP
.B F
Switch to fragmentation view.
On first press (or re-press), scans
.B /
with
.BR nftw (3)
and caches the result; subsequent renders display the cached data.
.TP
.B H
Toggle human-readable display
.TP
.B Q
Quit and restore terminal state
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid argument or system call failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List all mounted filesystems with human-readable sizes:
.B my_fs \-h
.TP
Check inode usage on the root filesystem:
.B my_fs \-i /
.TP
Show dual-perspective Use% with reserved blocks (most informative on ext4):
.B my_fs \-rh /
.TP
Analyze extents of a single file:
.B my_fs \-f /etc/passwd
.TP
Scan fragmentation under a mount point:
.B my_fs \-F /
.TP
Launch TUI in human-readable mode:
.B my_fs \-sh
.SH IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Block size is taken from
.I f_frsize
(not
.IR f_bsize )
to avoid a 256x inflation bug on virtiofs mounts.
.IP \(bu 2
Use% formula: ceiling(used \[mu] 100 / (used + f_bavail)), matching GNU
.BR df (1) .
RUse% (\fB\-r\fR mode) uses ceiling(used \[mu] 100 / f_blocks), which includes
the root-reserved area.
.IP \(bu 2
FIEMAP is not supported on overlayfs, virtiofs, tmpfs, procfs, and other
pseudo-filesystems; these return an appropriate error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR filefrag (1),
.BR statfs (2),
.BR ioctl_fiemap (2),
.BR nftw (3)
.SH AUTHOR
YuC13600
